WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.068
Pronouns that hold on.

2
00:00:02.518 --> 00:00:05.674
Some pronouns are written joined
to the end of another word.

3
00:00:05.924 --> 00:00:06.700
His book.

4
00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:07.986
‫كِتَابُهُ‬

5
00:00:08.336 --> 00:00:08.998
On it.

6
00:00:09.248 --> 00:00:10.148
‫عَلَيْهِ‬

7
00:00:10.498 --> 00:00:11.392
He opened it.

8
00:00:11.642 --> 00:00:12.633
‫فَتَحَهُ‬

9
00:00:13.183 --> 00:00:15.563
Chapter one. The twelve attached pronouns.

10
00:00:16.013 --> 00:00:18.191
An attached pronoun cannot stand alone.

11
00:00:18.391 --> 00:00:21.439
It joins the end of a noun,
a preposition or a verb.

12
00:00:21.639 --> 00:00:23.876
Like the separate pronouns, it is fixed.

13
00:00:24.326 --> 00:00:25.529
Here are all twelve.

14
00:00:25.529 --> 00:00:30.400
Each row shows the pronoun, who it means,
the pronoun on a noun, and the English.

15
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:32.883
The pronoun for I, or me. My book.

16
00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:34.126
‫كِتَابِي‬

17
00:00:34.476 --> 00:00:36.702
The pronoun for we, or us. Our book.

18
00:00:36.952 --> 00:00:38.021
‫كِتَابُنَا‬

19
00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.634
The pronoun for you, one man. Your book.

20
00:00:40.884 --> 00:00:41.895
‫كِتَابُكَ‬

21
00:00:42.245 --> 00:00:44.560
The pronoun for you, one woman. Your book.

22
00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:45.873
‫كِتَابُكِ‬

23
00:00:46.223 --> 00:00:48.229
The pronoun for you, two. Your book.

24
00:00:48.479 --> 00:00:49.711
‫كِتَابُكُمَا‬

25
00:00:50.061 --> 00:00:53.193
The pronoun for you, men,
or a mixed group. Your book.

26
00:00:53.443 --> 00:00:54.630
‫كِتَابُكُمْ‬

27
00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:57.069
The pronoun for you, women. Your book.

28
00:00:57.319 --> 00:00:58.852
‫كِتَابُكُنَّ‬

29
00:00:59.202 --> 00:01:01.249
The pronoun for he, or it. His book.

30
00:01:01.499 --> 00:01:02.535
‫كِتَابُهُ‬

31
00:01:02.885 --> 00:01:04.910
The pronoun for she, or it. Her book.

32
00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.210
‫كِتَابُهَا‬

33
00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.748
The pronoun for they, two. Their book.

34
00:01:08.998 --> 00:01:10.242
‫كِتَابُهُمَا‬

35
00:01:10.592 --> 00:01:13.967
The pronoun for they, men,
or a mixed group. Their book.

36
00:01:14.217 --> 00:01:15.405
‫كِتَابُهُمْ‬

37
00:01:15.755 --> 00:01:17.994
The pronoun for they, women. Their book.

38
00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:19.758
‫كِتَابُهُنَّ‬

39
00:01:20.308 --> 00:01:23.684
Tip. Compare them with the
separate pronouns of unit one.

40
00:01:23.934 --> 00:01:24.941
‫أَنْتُمَا‬

41
00:01:25.291 --> 00:01:27.260
and the attached pronoun for you, two.

42
00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:28.482
‫أَنْتُمْ‬

43
00:01:28.832 --> 00:01:31.847
and the attached pronoun for
you, men or a mixed group.

44
00:01:32.097 --> 00:01:33.351
‫أَنْتُنَّ‬

45
00:01:33.701 --> 00:01:35.760
and the attached pronoun for you, women.

46
00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:38.017
The family of this pronoun means you.

47
00:01:38.217 --> 00:01:40.489
The family of this one
means he, she and they.

48
00:01:42.733 --> 00:01:44.964
Chapter two. On a noun: the owner.

49
00:01:45.414 --> 00:01:47.552
A pronoun on a noun shows who owns it.

50
00:01:47.702 --> 00:01:50.043
It works like the second word of an iḍāfa.

51
00:01:50.393 --> 00:01:51.350
Zayd's book.

52
00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:52.996
‫كِتَابُ زَيْدٍ‬

53
00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:54.122
His book.

54
00:01:54.372 --> 00:01:55.408
‫كِتَابُهُ‬

55
00:01:55.758 --> 00:01:57.630
Zayd is the owner, so it is jarr.

56
00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:59.524
The pronoun for he takes its job.

57
00:01:59.874 --> 00:02:01.000
His book is new.

58
00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:03.028
‫كِتَابُهُ جَدِيدٌ‬

59
00:02:03.378 --> 00:02:04.886
The pronoun for he is the owner.

60
00:02:05.036 --> 00:02:09.550
It is fixed, so it does not change its
ending. It is in the place of jarr.

61
00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:11.921
‫فِي مَحَلِّ جَرٍّ‬

62
00:02:12.271 --> 00:02:13.519
Her house is near.

63
00:02:13.769 --> 00:02:15.584
‫بَيْتُهَا قَرِيبٌ‬

64
00:02:15.934 --> 00:02:18.832
The pronoun for she is the
owner, in the place of jarr.

65
00:02:19.282 --> 00:02:20.533
No al, no tanween.

66
00:02:20.733 --> 00:02:24.400
A noun with an attached pronoun
is the first word of an iḍāfa.

67
00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:26.347
So it has no al and no tanween.

68
00:02:26.597 --> 00:02:27.280
A book,

69
00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:28.444
‫كِتَابٌ‬

70
00:02:28.794 --> 00:02:29.940
becomes his book.

71
00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:31.226
‫كِتَابُهُ‬

72
00:02:31.776 --> 00:02:34.564
The noun still shows its own
ending before the pronoun.

73
00:02:34.714 --> 00:02:37.833
Only the noun is flexible.
The pronoun stays the same.

74
00:02:38.183 --> 00:02:39.309
His book is new.

75
00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:41.337
‫كِتَابُهُ جَدِيدٌ‬

76
00:02:41.687 --> 00:02:44.831
The word for book is the
Topic. It is rafʿ, with damma.

77
00:02:45.081 --> 00:02:45.930
‫كِتَابُ‬

78
00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:47.639
The student read his book.

79
00:02:47.889 --> 00:02:50.486
‫قَرَأَ الطَّالِبُ كِتَابَهُ‬

80
00:02:50.836 --> 00:02:54.040
The word for book is the
object. It is naṣb, with fatha.

81
00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:55.138
‫كِتَابَ‬

82
00:02:55.488 --> 00:02:56.796
The pen is in his book.

83
00:02:57.046 --> 00:02:59.414
‫القَلَمُ فِي كِتَابِهِ‬

84
00:02:59.764 --> 00:03:04.722
The word for book comes after the preposition
meaning in. It is jarr, with kasra.

85
00:03:04.972 --> 00:03:05.877
‫كِتَابِ‬

86
00:03:06.427 --> 00:03:09.817
A spelling tip. Look at a
word that ends in this letter.

87
00:03:09.967 --> 00:03:13.149
Before a pronoun, it is
written as this letter instead.

88
00:03:13.399 --> 00:03:14.149
A car.

89
00:03:14.399 --> 00:03:15.475
‫سَيَّارَةٌ‬

90
00:03:15.825 --> 00:03:16.727
His car.

91
00:03:16.977 --> 00:03:18.185
‫سَيَّارَتُهُ‬

92
00:03:18.535 --> 00:03:19.278
A room.

93
00:03:19.528 --> 00:03:20.591
‫غُرْفَةٌ‬

94
00:03:20.941 --> 00:03:21.698
Her room.

95
00:03:21.948 --> 00:03:23.022
‫غُرْفَتُهَا‬

96
00:03:25.266 --> 00:03:26.204
Chapter three.

97
00:03:26.354 --> 00:03:28.593
With the pronoun for me,
the ending is hidden.

98
00:03:29.043 --> 00:03:31.749
The pronoun for me always
needs a kasra before it.

99
00:03:31.899 --> 00:03:35.231
So the noun cannot show damma,
fatha or kasra of its own.

100
00:03:35.581 --> 00:03:36.549
My book is new.

101
00:03:36.799 --> 00:03:38.551
‫كِتَابِي جَدِيدٌ‬

102
00:03:38.901 --> 00:03:43.072
The word for book is the Topic, and
it is rafʿ. But you see a kasra.

103
00:03:43.422 --> 00:03:44.693
The pen is in my book.

104
00:03:44.943 --> 00:03:47.257
‫القَلَمُ فِي كِتَابِي‬

105
00:03:47.607 --> 00:03:50.652
Here the word for book is
jarr. It looks the same.

106
00:03:51.102 --> 00:03:55.040
So here is the rule. Do not read the
ending before the pronoun for me.

107
00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:57.304
Before it, the kasra is for the pronoun.

108
00:03:57.504 --> 00:04:01.001
Find the job of the noun from the
sentence, never from this vowel.

109
00:04:03.266 --> 00:04:05.492
Chapter four. On a preposition.

110
00:04:05.942 --> 00:04:10.623
A pronoun after a preposition is jarr,
like any word after a preposition.

111
00:04:10.773 --> 00:04:13.074
It is fixed, so it is
in the place of jarr.

112
00:04:13.424 --> 00:04:15.449
The pen is yours. That is, for you.

113
00:04:15.699 --> 00:04:17.122
‫القَلَمُ لَكَ‬

114
00:04:17.472 --> 00:04:21.301
The pronoun for you, one man, comes
after the preposition meaning for.

115
00:04:21.351 --> 00:04:23.358
That preposition is only one letter.

116
00:04:23.408 --> 00:04:25.174
The pronoun is in the place of jarr.

117
00:04:25.524 --> 00:04:26.552
He went out of it.

118
00:04:26.802 --> 00:04:28.190
‫خَرَجَ مِنْهُ‬

119
00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:31.705
The pronoun for it comes after
the preposition meaning from.

120
00:04:31.955 --> 00:04:32.675
‫مِنْ‬

121
00:04:32.925 --> 00:04:34.609
It is in the place of jarr too.

122
00:04:34.959 --> 00:04:35.965
The book is on it.

123
00:04:36.215 --> 00:04:37.942
‫الكِتَابُ عَلَيْهِ‬

124
00:04:38.292 --> 00:04:41.711
Here the pronoun for it comes
after the preposition meaning on.

125
00:04:41.961 --> 00:04:42.681
‫عَلَى‬

126
00:04:42.931 --> 00:04:48.719
It is in the place of jarr. Its kasra is
not a sign of jarr. Only the sound changes.

127
00:04:48.719 --> 00:04:50.442
Chapter five explains it.

128
00:04:50.892 --> 00:04:54.303
Some prepositions change their
shape. Learn these forms.

129
00:04:54.553 --> 00:04:59.931
Each row has the preposition, then the preposition
with the pronoun for he, for you, and for me.

130
00:05:00.181 --> 00:05:01.881
In. In it, in you, in me.

131
00:05:02.131 --> 00:05:02.841
‫فِي‬

132
00:05:03.041 --> 00:05:03.965
‫فِيهِ‬

133
00:05:04.165 --> 00:05:04.985
‫فِيكَ‬

134
00:05:05.185 --> 00:05:05.948
‫فِيَّ‬

135
00:05:06.398 --> 00:05:08.145
On. On it, on you, on me.

136
00:05:08.395 --> 00:05:09.115
‫عَلَى‬

137
00:05:09.315 --> 00:05:10.215
‫عَلَيْهِ‬

138
00:05:10.415 --> 00:05:11.321
‫عَلَيْكَ‬

139
00:05:11.521 --> 00:05:12.261
‫عَلَيَّ‬

140
00:05:12.711 --> 00:05:14.431
To. To it, to you, to me.

141
00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:15.377
‫إِلَى‬

142
00:05:15.577 --> 00:05:16.538
‫إِلَيْهِ‬

143
00:05:16.738 --> 00:05:17.702
‫إِلَيْكَ‬

144
00:05:17.902 --> 00:05:18.766
‫إِلَيَّ‬

145
00:05:19.216 --> 00:05:21.438
From. From it, from you, from me.

146
00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:22.408
‫مِنْ‬

147
00:05:22.608 --> 00:05:23.448
‫مِنْهُ‬

148
00:05:23.648 --> 00:05:24.481
‫مِنْكَ‬

149
00:05:24.681 --> 00:05:25.471
‫مِنِّي‬

150
00:05:25.921 --> 00:05:29.837
For. This one is a single
letter. For him, for you, for me.

151
00:05:30.087 --> 00:05:30.857
‫لَهُ‬

152
00:05:31.057 --> 00:05:31.859
‫لَكَ‬

153
00:05:32.059 --> 00:05:32.788
‫لِي‬

154
00:05:33.338 --> 00:05:34.826
Three changes to remember.

155
00:05:35.076 --> 00:05:37.092
One. The preposition meaning on.

156
00:05:37.342 --> 00:05:38.062
‫عَلَى‬

157
00:05:38.312 --> 00:05:40.950
Before a pronoun, its end
changes to this shape.

158
00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:41.762
On it.

159
00:05:42.012 --> 00:05:42.912
‫عَلَيْهِ‬

160
00:05:43.262 --> 00:05:45.308
Two. The preposition meaning to.

161
00:05:45.558 --> 00:05:46.254
‫إِلَى‬

162
00:05:46.504 --> 00:05:48.226
Its end changes in the same way.

163
00:05:48.376 --> 00:05:49.115
To her.

164
00:05:49.365 --> 00:05:50.439
‫إِلَيْهَا‬

165
00:05:50.789 --> 00:05:54.393
Three. The preposition meaning
for is one letter with a kasra.

166
00:05:54.543 --> 00:05:56.640
Before a pronoun, it takes a fatha.

167
00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:58.229
For him, for you, for her.

168
00:05:58.479 --> 00:05:59.249
‫لَهُ‬

169
00:05:59.449 --> 00:06:00.251
‫لَكَ‬

170
00:06:00.451 --> 00:06:01.249
‫لَهَا‬

171
00:06:01.599 --> 00:06:05.086
Only with the pronoun for me
does it keep its kasra. For me.

172
00:06:05.336 --> 00:06:06.065
‫لِي‬

173
00:06:08.299 --> 00:06:10.621
Chapter five. When the pronoun for he

174
00:06:10.621 --> 00:06:12.467
changes its damma to a kasra.

175
00:06:12.917 --> 00:06:14.960
After a kasra, or after this letter,

176
00:06:15.010 --> 00:06:17.661
the damma of the pronoun
for he becomes a kasra.

177
00:06:17.911 --> 00:06:20.158
After this letter: in it, on it, to him.

178
00:06:20.408 --> 00:06:21.332
‫فِيهِ‬

179
00:06:21.532 --> 00:06:22.432
‫عَلَيْهِ‬

180
00:06:22.632 --> 00:06:23.593
‫إِلَيْهِ‬

181
00:06:23.943 --> 00:06:26.257
After a kasra: with it, and in his house.

182
00:06:26.507 --> 00:06:27.304
‫بِهِ‬

183
00:06:27.504 --> 00:06:28.922
‫فِي بَيْتِهِ‬

184
00:06:29.472 --> 00:06:31.630
The same happens to three more pronouns.

185
00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:32.554
They, two.

186
00:06:32.654 --> 00:06:33.434
They, men.

187
00:06:33.534 --> 00:06:34.408
And they, women.

188
00:06:34.758 --> 00:06:35.458
On them.

189
00:06:35.708 --> 00:06:36.715
‫عَلَيْهِمْ‬

190
00:06:37.065 --> 00:06:38.603
The pronoun for they, men,

191
00:06:38.603 --> 00:06:40.091
comes after this letter,

192
00:06:40.091 --> 00:06:41.928
so its damma becomes a kasra.

193
00:06:42.278 --> 00:06:43.072
In them, two.

194
00:06:43.322 --> 00:06:44.382
‫فِيهِمَا‬

195
00:06:44.732 --> 00:06:46.219
The pronoun for they, two,

196
00:06:46.219 --> 00:06:47.837
comes after the same letter,

197
00:06:47.837 --> 00:06:49.603
so it changes in the same way.

198
00:06:49.953 --> 00:06:51.250
In their house, women.

199
00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:53.275
‫فِي بَيْتِهِنَّ‬

200
00:06:53.625 --> 00:06:56.152
The word for house ends in a kasra here.

201
00:06:56.152 --> 00:06:58.932
It is jarr after the
preposition meaning in.

202
00:06:58.982 --> 00:07:01.323
The pronoun for they,
women, comes after it,

203
00:07:01.323 --> 00:07:03.347
so its damma becomes a kasra too.

204
00:07:03.797 --> 00:07:05.682
Tip. It is the same pronoun.

205
00:07:05.832 --> 00:07:08.554
Only the sound changes,
to make it easy to say.

206
00:07:08.804 --> 00:07:12.467
With a damma, a fatha or a sukūn
before it, it stays as it is.

207
00:07:12.717 --> 00:07:14.267
After a sukūn: from him.

208
00:07:14.517 --> 00:07:15.357
‫مِنْهُ‬

209
00:07:15.707 --> 00:07:17.063
After a fatha: for him.

210
00:07:17.313 --> 00:07:18.083
‫لَهُ‬

211
00:07:18.433 --> 00:07:19.956
After a damma: his book.

212
00:07:20.206 --> 00:07:21.242
‫كِتَابُهُ‬

213
00:07:23.499 --> 00:07:25.849
Chapter six. On a verb: the object.

214
00:07:26.299 --> 00:07:31.281
Put one of the twelve pronouns on a past
verb or an order verb, and it is the object.

215
00:07:31.431 --> 00:07:32.767
The object is naṣb.

216
00:07:32.917 --> 00:07:35.928
The pronoun is fixed, so
it is in the place of naṣb.

217
00:07:36.178 --> 00:07:38.321
‫فِي مَحَلِّ نَصْبٍ‬

218
00:07:38.871 --> 00:07:39.998
He opened the door.

219
00:07:40.248 --> 00:07:41.629
‫فَتَحَ البَابَ‬

220
00:07:41.979 --> 00:07:42.873
He opened it.

221
00:07:43.123 --> 00:07:44.114
‫فَتَحَهُ‬

222
00:07:44.464 --> 00:07:46.666
The pronoun for it takes
the place of the door.

223
00:07:46.916 --> 00:07:47.802
‫البَابَ‬

224
00:07:48.252 --> 00:07:49.353
The girl opened it.

225
00:07:49.603 --> 00:07:51.518
‫فَتَحَتْهُ البِنْتُ‬

226
00:07:51.868 --> 00:07:54.609
The pronoun comes right after
the verb, before the doer.

227
00:07:55.059 --> 00:07:57.302
The teacher wrote it. It means the letter.

228
00:07:57.552 --> 00:07:59.631
‫كَتَبَهَا المُدَرِّسُ‬

229
00:07:59.981 --> 00:08:03.390
In Arabic, the word for a
letter you write is feminine.

230
00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:05.249
So we use the pronoun for she.

231
00:08:05.399 --> 00:08:07.552
It is the object, in the place of naṣb.

232
00:08:08.002 --> 00:08:08.832
Read the book.

233
00:08:09.082 --> 00:08:10.605
‫اِقْرَأِ الكِتَابَ‬

234
00:08:10.955 --> 00:08:11.621
Read it.

235
00:08:11.871 --> 00:08:12.876
‫اِقْرَأْهُ‬

236
00:08:13.226 --> 00:08:18.305
Before al, the order verb had a small
helping kasra, only to make it easy to say.

237
00:08:18.305 --> 00:08:19.245
It is not jarr.

238
00:08:19.395 --> 00:08:22.083
With the pronoun, the
order verb keeps its sukūn.

239
00:08:22.333 --> 00:08:23.241
‫اِقْرَأْ‬

240
00:08:23.391 --> 00:08:25.136
Then the pronoun for it is added.

241
00:08:25.586 --> 00:08:26.295
Write it.

242
00:08:26.545 --> 00:08:27.607
‫اُكْتُبْهُ‬

243
00:08:27.957 --> 00:08:30.964
The pronoun for it is the
object, in the place of naṣb.

244
00:08:31.414 --> 00:08:34.326
Tip. Past verbs also have
endings for the doer.

245
00:08:34.476 --> 00:08:35.121
I,

246
00:08:35.171 --> 00:08:35.874
you,

247
00:08:35.924 --> 00:08:36.667
and we.

248
00:08:36.917 --> 00:08:39.920
They are pronouns too. We
learn them in unit six.

249
00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:44.434
One more tip. On a verb, the
pronoun for me has an extra letter.

250
00:08:44.484 --> 00:08:45.230
This one.

251
00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:46.402
We meet it later.

252
00:08:48.666 --> 00:08:51.032
Chapter seven. Three places, one table.

253
00:08:51.482 --> 00:08:55.893
Here is the whole lesson in one
table. What is the pronoun joined to?

254
00:08:55.893 --> 00:08:58.259
What is its job? What place is it in?

255
00:08:58.609 --> 00:09:02.794
Joined to a noun, it is the owner,
in the place of jarr. His book.

256
00:09:03.044 --> 00:09:04.080
‫كِتَابُهُ‬

257
00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:08.676
Joined to a preposition, its job
is called after a preposition.

258
00:09:08.676 --> 00:09:10.967
It is in the place of jarr. On it.

259
00:09:11.217 --> 00:09:12.117
‫عَلَيْهِ‬

260
00:09:12.467 --> 00:09:16.895
Joined to a past or order verb, it
is the object, in the place of naṣb.

261
00:09:16.895 --> 00:09:17.706
He opened it.

262
00:09:17.956 --> 00:09:18.947
‫فَتَحَهُ‬

263
00:09:19.297 --> 00:09:20.947
And with an order verb, read it.

264
00:09:21.197 --> 00:09:22.202
‫اِقْرَأْهُ‬

265
00:09:22.752 --> 00:09:23.604
In short.

266
00:09:23.854 --> 00:09:25.985
There are twelve attached pronouns.

267
00:09:25.985 --> 00:09:30.065
One for I, one for we, five for
you, and five for he, she and they.

268
00:09:30.415 --> 00:09:34.057
On a noun, the pronoun is the
owner, in the place of jarr.

269
00:09:34.057 --> 00:09:35.941
The noun loses al and tanween.

270
00:09:36.291 --> 00:09:40.868
After a preposition, it is in the
place of jarr. On it, to you, for him.

271
00:09:41.118 --> 00:09:42.018
‫عَلَيْهِ‬

272
00:09:42.218 --> 00:09:43.182
‫إِلَيْكَ‬

273
00:09:43.382 --> 00:09:44.152
‫لَهُ‬

274
00:09:44.502 --> 00:09:48.299
On a verb, it is the object, in
the place of naṣb. He opened it.

275
00:09:48.549 --> 00:09:49.540
‫فَتَحَهُ‬

276
00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:51.008
The pronoun for he

277
00:09:51.008 --> 00:09:54.454
changes its damma to a kasra
after a kasra or this letter.

278
00:09:54.704 --> 00:09:57.513
And before the pronoun for me,
the noun's ending is hidden.

279
00:09:57.963 --> 00:10:01.384
Well done. Now open the Practice
tab and try it yourself.
